{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a user leaves your application and returns and the query data is stale, "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Query automatically requests fresh data for you in the background"}]},{"type":"text","value":". You can disable this globally or per-query using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refetchOnWindowFocus"},{"type":"text","value":" option:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"disabling-globally","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disabling Globally"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientConfig: {\n    defaultOptions: {\n      queries: {\n        refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)","lang":"js"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"disabling-per-query","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disabling Per-Query"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: fetchTodos,\n  refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"custom-window-focus-event","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Window Focus Event"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In rare circumstances, you may want to manage your own window focus events that trigger TanStack Query to revalidate. To do this, TanStack Query provides a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusManager.setEventListener"},{"type":"text","value":" function that supplies you the callback that should be fired when the window is focused and allows you to set up your own events. When calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusManager.setEventListener"},{"type":"text","value":", the previously set handler is removed (which in most cases will be the default handler) and your new handler is used instead. For example, this is the default handler:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"focusManager.setEventListener((handleFocus) => {\n  // Listen to visibilitychange and focus\n  if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.addEventListener) {\n    window.addEventListener('visibilitychange', handleFocus, false)\n    window.addEventListener('focus', handleFocus, false)\n  }\n\n  return () => {\n    // Be sure to unsubscribe if a new handler is set\n    window.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', handleFocus)\n    window.removeEventListener('focus', handleFocus)\n  }\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ignoring-iframe-focus-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ignoring Iframe Focus Events"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A great use-case for replacing the focus handler is that of iframe events. Iframes present problems with detecting window focus by both double-firing events and also firing false-positive events when focusing or using iframes within your app. If you experience this, you should use an event handler that ignores these events as much as possible. I recommend "},{"type":"link","href":"https://gist.github.com/tannerlinsley/1d3a2122332107fcd8c9cc379be10d88","children":[{"type":"text","value":"this one"}]},{"type":"text","value":"! It can be set up in the following way:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { focusManager } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\nimport onWindowFocus from './onWindowFocus' // The gist above\n\nfocusManager.setEventListener(onWindowFocus) // Boom!","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"managing-focus-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Managing focus state"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { focusManager } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\n// Override the default focus state\nfocusManager.setFocused(true)\n\n// Fallback to the default focus check\nfocusManager.setFocused(undefined)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pitfalls-caveats","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pitfalls & Caveats"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some browser internal dialogue windows, such as spawned by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alert()"},{"type":"text","value":" or file upload dialogues (as created by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<input type=\"file\" />"},{"type":"text","value":") might also trigger focus refetching after they close. This can result in unwanted side effects, as the refetching might trigger component unmounts or remounts before your file upload handler is executed. See "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/tannerlinsley/react-query/issues/2960","children":[{"type":"text","value":"this issue on GitHub"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for background and possible workarounds."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"disabling-globally","text":"Disabling Globally","level":4},{"id":"disabling-per-query","text":"Disabling Per-Query","level":4},{"id":"custom-window-focus-event","text":"Custom Window Focus Event","level":2},{"id":"ignoring-iframe-focus-events","text":"Ignoring Iframe Focus Events","level":2},{"id":"managing-focus-state","text":"Managing focus state","level":2},{"id":"pitfalls-caveats","text":"Pitfalls & Caveats","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nIf a user leaves your application and returns and the query data is stale, **TanStack Query automatically requests fresh data for you in the background**. You can disable this globally or per-query using the `refetchOnWindowFocus` option:\n\n#### Disabling Globally\n\n\n\n```js\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientConfig: {\n    defaultOptions: {\n      queries: {\n        refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)\n```\n\n\n\n#### Disabling Per-Query\n\n\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: fetchTodos,\n  refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n})\n```\n\n\n\n## Custom Window Focus Event\n\nIn rare circumstances, you may want to manage your own window focus events that trigger TanStack Query to revalidate. To do this, TanStack Query provides a `focusManager.setEventListener` function that supplies you the callback that should be fired when the window is focused and allows you to set up your own events. When calling `focusManager.setEventListener`, the previously set handler is removed (which in most cases will be the default handler) and your new handler is used instead. For example, this is the default handler:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nfocusManager.setEventListener((handleFocus) => {\n  // Listen to visibilitychange and focus\n  if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.addEventListener) {\n    window.addEventListener('visibilitychange', handleFocus, false)\n    window.addEventListener('focus', handleFocus, false)\n  }\n\n  return () => {\n    // Be sure to unsubscribe if a new handler is set\n    window.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', handleFocus)\n    window.removeEventListener('focus', handleFocus)\n  }\n})\n```\n\n\n\n## Ignoring Iframe Focus Events\n\nA great use-case for replacing the focus handler is that of iframe events. Iframes present problems with detecting window focus by both double-firing events and also firing false-positive events when focusing or using iframes within your app. If you experience this, you should use an event handler that ignores these events as much as possible. I recommend [this one](https://gist.github.com/tannerlinsley/1d3a2122332107fcd8c9cc379be10d88)! It can be set up in the following way:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nimport { focusManager } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\nimport onWindowFocus from './onWindowFocus' // The gist above\n\nfocusManager.setEventListener(onWindowFocus) // Boom!\n```\n\n\n\n\n\n## Managing focus state\n\n\n\n```tsx\nimport { focusManager } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\n// Override the default focus state\nfocusManager.setFocused(true)\n\n// Fallback to the default focus check\nfocusManager.setFocused(undefined)\n```\n\n\n\n## Pitfalls & Caveats\n\nSome browser internal dialogue windows, such as spawned by `alert()` or file upload dialogues (as created by `<input type=\"file\" />`) might also trigger focus refetching after they close. This can result in unwanted side effects, as the refetching might trigger component unmounts or remounts before your file upload handler is executed. See [this issue on GitHub](https://github.com/tannerlinsley/react-query/issues/2960) for background and possible workarounds.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: window-focus-refetching\ntitle: Window Focus Refetching\nref: docs/framework/react/guides/window-focus-refetching.md\nreplace: { '@tanstack/react-query': '@tanstack/vue-query' }\n---\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n\n```js\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientConfig: {\n    defaultOptions: {\n      queries: {\n        refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n[//]: # 'ReactNative'\n[//]: # 'ReactNative'\n"}
